WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:54.030 --> 01:58.060
<b>We’re at #29 for the ranking of the Yokohama
Arc Best Street Corner Countdown today...</b>

01:58.060 --> 02:00.630
<b>...at an underpass in Sakuragi Town.</b>

02:00.630 --> 02:02.830
<b>Please take a look at this street art.</b>

02:02.830 --> 02:06.440
<b>This was all allowed to be painted here, of course.</b>

02:06.440 --> 02:10.310
<b>The mural you see here
is a full kilometer long!</b>

02:10.310 --> 02:14.610
<b>These murals began appearing under
girder bridges in the late 1970s.</b>

02:14.610 --> 02:20.920
<b>Local pop artists started using the underpass
walls as canvases for murals like this.</b>

02:22.250 --> 02:26.190
<b>It feels like this section of the city
isn’t really part of Japan at all.</b>

02:26.190 --> 02:29.430
<b>The art you see here is very surreal, don’t you think?</b>

02:29.430 --> 02:32.730
<b>I wonder what type of person painted this?</b>

02:38.470 --> 02:45.440
<b>The Fish That Grew Wings</b>

02:55.320 --> 02:57.520
<b>Excuse me...</b>

02:57.520 --> 02:59.160
<b>What can I help you with?</b>

02:59.160 --> 03:02.330
<b>Do you think it’d be possible to
find out who painted this?</b>

03:02.330 --> 03:04.500
<b>That’d be pretty difficult, I think...</b>

03:04.500 --> 03:07.630
<b>The murals here are always painted
before anyone realizes...</b>

03:07.630 --> 03:09.970
<b>...and they’re gone before anyone realizes, too.</b>

03:09.970 --> 03:12.240
<b>Is that so...?</b>

03:12.970 --> 03:16.040
<b>This sure is a surrealistic picture, huh?</b>

03:16.040 --> 03:18.940
<b>Do you know what the “sur” in surrealism means?</b>

03:21.480 --> 03:23.150
<b>Strange...</b>

03:23.150 --> 03:25.880
<b>Different from the normal and ordinary...
Is that what you mean?</b>

03:26.450 --> 03:30.620
<b>In French, “sur” means “real.”</b>

03:30.620 --> 03:31.860
<b>“Real”?</b>

03:31.860 --> 03:37.830
<b>The “real” I’m talking about is the one kids
might use in lines like “that’s real cute.”</b>

03:38.400 --> 03:42.100
<b>So, surrealism is <i>real</i> realistic.</b>

03:43.300 --> 03:45.140
<b>Without being held captive to reason...</b>

03:45.140 --> 03:50.140
<b>By expressing yourself illogically with
your dreams and fantasies...</b>

03:50.140 --> 03:52.080
<b>...you can liberate yourself from
the known human world.</b>

03:52.980 --> 03:56.110
<b>Between the two World Wars in the 20th century,</b>

03:56.110 --> 03:58.920
<b>this movement happened
all over the world.</b>

03:58.920 --> 04:02.750
<b>I wonder if this mural is part of that movement?</b>

04:03.520 --> 04:05.420
<b>I don’t think so...</b>

04:17.070 --> 04:18.440
<b>Why...?</b>

04:19.670 --> 04:21.110
<b>Why?!</b>

04:22.570 --> 04:24.710
<b>This is the worst!</b>

04:27.950 --> 04:29.280
<b>I’m such a moron!</b>

05:10.990 --> 05:15.230
<b>The phone you are trying to reach
is either out of range or–</b>

05:19.970 --> 05:22.230
<b>Hey, did something happen?</b>

05:22.230 --> 05:23.400
<b>Why do you ask?</b>

05:23.400 --> 05:24.640
<b>Female intuition.</b>

05:24.640 --> 05:26.440
<b>Is that really it?</b>

05:26.440 --> 05:29.810
<b>Sukawara Akira gave us a call.</b>

05:29.810 --> 05:31.380
<b>She called your house?</b>

05:31.380 --> 05:35.410
<b>Well, the Miyama Store number
is in the phone book, so...</b>

05:35.950 --> 05:38.220
<b>Did she ask you about me?</b>

05:38.220 --> 05:41.320
<b>Yeah. Not only that, she asked me point blank...</b>

05:41.320 --> 05:44.390
<b>...how she could contact you.</b>

05:44.390 --> 05:49.460
<b>I wonder if she really thought I’d say
“yeah, sure,” and tell her just like that.</b>

05:49.460 --> 05:51.360
<b>Something happened over there,
didn’t it?</b>

05:51.360 --> 05:54.570
<b>I’ll tell you after I think on it a little more.</b>

05:54.570 --> 05:57.330
<b>I’m still a little confused about it myself.</b>

05:57.970 --> 06:00.300
<b>Are you all right?</b>

06:00.310 --> 06:01.510
<b>Yeah.</b>

06:01.510 --> 06:05.840
<b>If Sukawara calls again,
what should I say?</b>

06:05.840 --> 06:08.510
<b>You can give her my cell number.</b>

06:08.510 --> 06:09.510
<b>Okay.</b>

06:09.510 --> 06:12.880
<b>Er, she actually gave me her
cell number, but...</b>

06:15.150 --> 06:18.620
<b>Hey? You still there?</b>

06:32.300 --> 06:34.240
<b>It’s certainly been a while, hasn’t it?</b>

06:35.270 --> 06:36.110
<b>Is that you, Asako?</b>

06:36.880 --> 06:38.640
<b>Hana-san...</b>

06:38.640 --> 06:40.440
<b>I see you haven’t changed a bit.</b>

06:40.450 --> 06:42.250
<b>As if I would.</b>

06:42.250 --> 06:47.420
<b>It’s only been a few years since
you came here every day.</b>

06:47.420 --> 06:50.720
<b>Only a few years, huh?</b>

06:51.220 --> 06:54.960
<b>I’m sure you didn’t come all the way
from Tana just to see me, did you?</b>

06:54.960 --> 06:56.930
<b>No, but I figured since I was here...</b>

06:56.930 --> 07:00.130
<b>Have a seat.
I’ll put on some coffee.</b>

07:06.040 --> 07:06.870
<b>So?</b>

07:09.610 --> 07:14.480
<b>And after that, you said the warm-colored
light balls flew off somewhere, right?</b>

07:14.480 --> 07:15.550
<b>Are you absolutely sure?</b>

07:15.550 --> 07:16.950
<b>Yeah...</b>

07:16.950 --> 07:20.680
<b>It was really bright,
so I turned my head away...</b>

07:20.690 --> 07:25.490
<b>...and saw two of the lights flying off that way.</b>

07:25.490 --> 07:29.730
<b>So the warm-colored lights
destroyed a cold-colored light...</b>

07:29.730 --> 07:34.870
<b>I wonder if this really means that the two
types are competing with each other...</b>

07:34.870 --> 07:36.100
<b>Competing with each other?</b>

07:36.100 --> 07:39.670
<b>Well, since they’re cold and warm lights...</b>

07:39.670 --> 07:42.210
<b>Like in “The Wind and the Sun.”</b>

07:42.210 --> 07:43.870
<b>By Aesop?</b>

07:43.880 --> 07:45.540
<b>I could be wrong...</b>

07:45.540 --> 07:48.210
<b>No... I don’t think you’re that far off.</b>

07:49.650 --> 07:52.520
<b>If that were the case... what could
they be competing over?</b>

07:52.520 --> 07:55.920
<b>Well, certainly not a traveler’s cloak like in the story.</b>

07:59.260 --> 08:00.220
<b>What?</b>

08:00.790 --> 08:03.390
<b>I wonder which type Rieko-chan saw...</b>

08:04.560 --> 08:08.100
<b>Okay! Spill it, boy.</b>

08:10.700 --> 08:16.110
<b>If you say so, then that picture was
definitely done by that man.</b>

08:17.640 --> 08:20.180
<b>And I wanted to forget
all about him, too...</b>

08:23.520 --> 08:26.720
<b>But after I saw that picture,
it all came back to me in force.</b>

08:28.390 --> 08:30.820
<b>Even though I was trying hard to forget...</b>

08:30.820 --> 08:33.820
<b>...I might have just been throwing
a dust cover over my memories.</b>

08:35.430 --> 08:38.600
<b>Hana-san, do you know anything
about him right now?</b>

08:38.600 --> 08:39.960
<b>Let’s see...</b>

08:39.970 --> 08:43.970
<b>He hasn’t showed his face around here since then.</b>

08:43.970 --> 08:48.840
<b>Did you shamelessly come all the way back to
Yokohama to see your old boyfriend again?</b>

08:50.340 --> 08:51.680
<b>No...</b>

08:51.680 --> 08:55.050
<b>I don’t think that’s it...</b>

08:55.050 --> 08:57.010
<b>I was tracing the roots of my past...</b>

08:57.020 --> 08:59.450
<b>...and want to reexamine myself
as I am now because of them.</b>

09:01.950 --> 09:04.490
<b>It just might be the time for that...</b>

09:05.920 --> 09:11.400
<b>So the mischievous Asako-san has already become someone who says things like that?</b>

09:11.400 --> 09:13.730
<b>There’s nothing that doesn’t change.</b>

09:13.730 --> 09:16.730
<b>You’re the one who taught me that.</b>

09:25.240 --> 09:26.510
<b>What is it?</b>

09:26.510 --> 09:29.510
<b>I’m... going to split for today...</b>

09:29.510 --> 09:31.280
<b>She’s your friend, isn’t she?</b>

09:31.280 --> 09:33.020
<b>Let’s go see her together.</b>

09:33.020 --> 09:34.990
<b>But...</b>

09:34.990 --> 09:37.920
<b>...Rieko-chan doesn’t like me too much right now, so...</b>

09:39.830 --> 09:43.030
<b>Heeeeey. Booooy.</b>

09:54.170 --> 09:55.540
<b>Ah, hey...</b>

10:00.710 --> 10:02.080
<b>Umm...</b>

10:04.450 --> 10:05.220
<b>Here you go.</b>

10:05.220 --> 10:06.520
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

10:27.170 --> 10:29.310
<b>You saw both types, then?</b>

10:29.310 --> 10:30.110
<b>Yeah.</b>

10:30.110 --> 10:33.580
<b>And it looked like they were fighting?</b>

10:33.580 --> 10:34.710
<b>Yeah.</b>

10:34.710 --> 10:37.110
<b>Could you go into a little more detail?</b>

10:38.080 --> 10:42.090
<b>Like, do you think anyone else was
there who also saw them?</b>

10:42.090 --> 10:46.020
<b>I... don’t really care much
about that anymore.</b>

10:46.020 --> 10:48.090
<b>Why are you so desperate about this?</b>

10:48.090 --> 10:48.690
<b>Desperate?</b>

10:49.230 --> 10:52.200
<b>It’s not really that big of a deal, right?</b>

10:52.200 --> 10:54.670
<b>Lots of more important things are out there, right?</b>

10:55.800 --> 10:59.340
<b>To me, this is the most monumental topic of my life.</b>

11:00.770 --> 11:04.140
<b>And if you ask me why,
it’s because we all saw it.</b>

11:04.140 --> 11:04.910
<b>You all?</b>

11:07.710 --> 11:12.850
<b>Makabe Masaki, Tanigawa Kisa,
Kobayakawa Shigeki, and...</b>

11:12.850 --> 11:15.050
<b>...me.</b>

11:15.050 --> 11:15.990
<b>You saw them?</b>

11:16.820 --> 11:18.060
<b>I did.</b>

11:22.260 --> 11:24.430
<b>Let’s exchange what we know about it.</b>

11:58.600 --> 12:01.530
<b>Who’s that? Someone you know, Ha-chan?</b>

12:01.530 --> 12:03.100
<b>Should I drive her away?</b>

12:26.860 --> 12:30.560
<b>I’ll have one medium classic blend
and one medium latte, please.</b>

12:31.700 --> 12:33.830
<b>That comes to 780 yen.</b>

12:34.300 --> 12:35.630
<b>And they changed that!</b>

12:35.630 --> 12:37.540
<b>So you’re gonna buy it?</b>

12:37.540 --> 12:38.700
<b>Well, it’s really cute, so...</b>

12:53.890 --> 12:57.760
<b>I never thought I’d see you again.</b>

13:03.100 --> 13:04.860
<b>I was guided to you...</b>

13:04.860 --> 13:08.770
<b>...by that mural,
and the winged fish drawings.</b>

13:09.800 --> 13:11.340
<b>It’s my lingering attachment to you...</b>

13:11.340 --> 13:16.970
<b>I thought you might notice, so I drew
the fish after finishing the mural.</b>

13:19.240 --> 13:21.750
<b>How’ve you been since then?</b>

13:21.750 --> 13:24.480
<b>I went back to my hometown.</b>

13:24.480 --> 13:26.920
<b>If I recall, it was somewhere
near Izu, right?</b>

13:36.460 --> 13:39.000
<b>What do you want to do now, Jiro-kun?</b>

13:41.270 --> 13:44.070
<b>I haven’t changed a bit since back then.</b>

13:44.070 --> 13:45.440
<b>I see.</b>

13:45.440 --> 13:49.870
<b>I think you understood that best
out of everyone, Asako.</b>

13:49.880 --> 13:51.180
<b>Really?</b>

13:51.180 --> 13:55.350
<b>Yeah. Without you, I couldn’t have
been the man I am today.</b>

13:56.080 --> 13:59.320
<b>If that were the case,
I wouldn’t have left you.</b>

14:14.200 --> 14:18.240
<b>The phone you are trying to reach
is either out of range or–</b>

14:26.950 --> 14:28.280
<b>Hello?</b>

14:28.280 --> 14:29.810
<b>Hey...</b>

14:29.820 --> 14:32.320
<b>Oh, it’s you, Riezo.</b>

14:32.820 --> 14:35.990
<b>Umm... Sukawara-san spoke
to me about some things...</b>

14:35.990 --> 14:37.660
<b>“Sukawara”?</b>

14:37.660 --> 14:40.420
<b>The woman who’s been hanging
around with Makki lately.</b>

14:44.800 --> 14:46.100
<b>Shigeki...</b>

14:46.100 --> 14:50.170
<b>I was worried that you might be depressed,
feeling like you’re responsible for what happened...</b>

14:50.170 --> 14:51.440
<b>So I called.</b>

14:51.970 --> 14:54.180
<b>It’s not your fault, Shigeki.</b>

14:54.180 --> 14:58.680
<b>But... I was the one who told Kisa
she should meet with that guy...</b>

14:58.680 --> 15:02.580
<b>But Kisa’s the one who decided
to meet with him, right?</b>

15:02.580 --> 15:05.050
<b>Yes, but... Kisa’s...</b>

15:05.050 --> 15:06.150
<b>Umm...</b>

15:06.950 --> 15:09.260
<b>I also saw them.</b>

15:09.260 --> 15:11.760
<b>Saw... what?</b>

15:12.260 --> 15:16.760
<b>A place where an orange light was fighting
with some pale blue lights...</b>

15:17.400 --> 15:18.730
<b>Do you wanna meet somewhere?</b>

15:18.730 --> 15:21.130
<b>I’d like to meet and talk
about things, but...</b>

15:22.330 --> 15:23.230
<b>Okay.</b>

15:24.740 --> 15:26.200
<b>Then...</b>

15:27.840 --> 15:29.940
<b>That’s what I don’t understand.</b>

15:29.940 --> 15:33.880
<b>I don’t understand why I lost you...</b>

15:33.880 --> 15:37.180
<b>What was wrong with me?</b>

15:37.180 --> 15:40.990
<b>It wasn’t about what was or wasn’t wrong with you...</b>

15:40.990 --> 15:42.390
<b>Then...</b>

15:42.390 --> 15:45.560
<b>Back then,
you were at the end of your line.</b>

15:45.560 --> 15:48.490
<b>So you wanted to abandon me when
I was at the end of my line?</b>

15:49.730 --> 15:51.800
<b>That’s not it...</b>

15:53.630 --> 15:56.800
<b>As an artist... as a human being...</b>

15:56.800 --> 15:59.370
<b>...I struggled at the end of my line.</b>

15:59.370 --> 16:02.740
<b>I thought there was nothing I could
do after you ran away from me.</b>

16:02.740 --> 16:04.380
<b>But...</b>

16:04.380 --> 16:07.510
<b>I’m telling you,
it’s not what you’re thinking.</b>

16:07.510 --> 16:09.710
<b>It’s not? How can it not be?</b>

16:10.450 --> 16:12.350
<b>Jiro-kun...</b>

16:12.350 --> 16:15.790
<b>You only depended on yourself when
you were at the end of your line.</b>

16:17.160 --> 16:18.560
<b>In the end...</b>

16:18.560 --> 16:23.930
<b>...I thought I was just playing some
game of make-believe with you.</b>

16:23.930 --> 16:29.170
<b>I know I’m saying some harsh things,
but once I thought that way...</b>

16:29.170 --> 16:30.840
<b>...it was all over.</b>

16:35.470 --> 16:37.040
<b>Wait.</b>

16:37.040 --> 16:43.150
<b>In your head, you have this image
of how artists are supposed to be.</b>

16:43.150 --> 16:45.080
<b>So when you were at the end
of your line...</b>

16:45.080 --> 16:48.950
<b>...you put yourself in that image,
and you were able to find relief.</b>

16:50.160 --> 16:53.360
<b>You have things backwards.</b>

16:53.360 --> 16:57.190
<b>People don’t create works
to be called artists.</b>

16:58.000 --> 17:02.200
<b>Just imagining them is enough to be
called an artist, don’t you think?</b>

17:02.200 --> 17:04.170
<b>Isn’t that right?</b>

17:04.170 --> 17:05.870
<b>You really are saying some harsh things.</b>

17:05.870 --> 17:06.900
<b>But I’m...</b>

17:06.910 --> 17:11.280
<b>Hatori Jiro, who has to shoulder
the modern art movement?</b>

17:29.460 --> 17:31.300
<b>Dosshiru.</b>

17:31.300 --> 17:33.230
<b>Shisshin.</b>

17:55.820 --> 17:58.420
<b>Hello? Sukawara speaking.</b>

17:58.420 --> 17:59.620
<b>Umm...</b>

17:59.620 --> 18:01.290
<b>Aizawa-kun?</b>

18:01.290 --> 18:02.160
<b>Yeah...</b>

18:02.160 --> 18:04.400
<b>I thought you’d get in touch
with me at some point!</b>

18:04.400 --> 18:05.900
<b>Wanna do this together?</b>

18:07.500 --> 18:08.970
<b>You’re interested in them, aren’t you?</b>

18:08.970 --> 18:12.500
<b>The warm-colored and cold-colored lights...</b>

18:12.500 --> 18:14.340
<b>And their rivalry.</b>

18:14.340 --> 18:17.340
<b>You called me because it’s on your mind, right?</b>

18:19.640 --> 18:22.610
<b>If you want to investigate them
together with me, call me back.</b>

18:22.610 --> 18:26.120
<b>That’s all I have to say for now.
Thanks for calling.</b>

18:48.270 --> 18:49.970
<b>That smoked eggplant...</b>

18:51.380 --> 18:53.780
<b>It... was pretty good.</b>

18:53.780 --> 18:55.010
<b>You always did love it.</b>

18:55.850 --> 18:58.250
<b>It really was good.</b>

18:58.250 --> 19:00.480
<b>Time glorifies people.</b>

19:00.490 --> 19:04.050
<b>Not necessarily.</b>

19:04.060 --> 19:06.720
<b>There are memories you can’t forget
no matter how much you try...</b>

19:06.730 --> 19:10.160
<b>...and memories you try so hard
to erase that won’t fade away.</b>

19:10.630 --> 19:11.730
<b>Hey...</b>

19:11.730 --> 19:17.270
<b>Why is the Hatori Jiro I once knew
living a homeless life out here?</b>

19:17.270 --> 19:19.400
<b>I’m...</b>

19:19.400 --> 19:21.770
<b>...not too sure myself.</b>

19:22.640 --> 19:27.650
<b>As soon as I put why I’m here
into words...</b>

19:27.650 --> 19:30.110
<b>...I instantly think it’s
for a different reason.</b>

19:30.120 --> 19:32.620
<b>Once I starting putting
the words together...</b>

19:32.620 --> 19:35.220
<b>...the more ambiguous my true reason becomes.</b>

19:36.250 --> 19:38.460
<b>I really don’t know.</b>

19:38.460 --> 19:39.190
<b>I see...</b>

19:39.990 --> 19:42.730
<b>That’s why I’m going to continue to paint.</b>

19:42.730 --> 19:45.130
<b>Until you find your answer.</b>

19:45.130 --> 19:46.530
<b>I guess that’s right.</b>

19:46.530 --> 19:47.500
<b>Yeah.</b>

19:48.330 --> 19:51.440
<b>If... you don’t find it,
what will you do?</b>

19:51.440 --> 19:53.300
<b>That would be okay, too.</b>

19:55.040 --> 19:56.410
<b>What?</b>

19:56.410 --> 19:58.640
<b>I just thought you’re doing pretty well
the way you are right now, Jiro-kun.</b>

20:02.610 --> 20:04.480
<b>Do you live near Hakone?</b>

20:04.480 --> 20:05.880
<b>I guess so.</b>

20:05.880 --> 20:08.490
<b>The Hakone Mountains are basically
right in front of where I live.</b>

20:08.490 --> 20:11.860
<b>I’ll be having an exhibition at a
Hakone gallery in the near future.</b>

20:11.860 --> 20:13.660
<b>Should I send you directions?</b>

20:13.660 --> 20:15.730
<b>No, I’ll look it up.</b>

20:15.730 --> 20:18.860
<b>If I can go, I will.</b>

20:18.860 --> 20:21.130
<b>Will you be there?</b>

20:24.440 --> 20:25.370
<b>Probably not.</b>

20:27.470 --> 20:29.340
<b>I’m glad I came.</b>

20:29.340 --> 20:32.180
<b>Yeah, I’m glad I was able
to see you again, too.</b>

20:32.180 --> 20:33.640
<b>Thank you.</b>

21:08.880 --> 21:10.650
<b>Hello?</b>

21:10.650 --> 21:12.350
<b>Where are you?</b>

21:12.350 --> 21:14.620
<b>Still home...</b>

21:14.620 --> 21:17.090
<b>I just haven’t been able to gather my thoughts...</b>

21:17.090 --> 21:20.060
<b>That’s why I think we should meet and talk it over.</b>

21:21.330 --> 21:23.290
<b>I want a little more time...</b>

21:23.760 --> 21:25.200
<b>Sorry for today...</b>

21:37.710 --> 21:41.210
<b>The phone you are trying to reach
is either out of range or–</b>

22:14.910 --> 22:16.210
<b>Stick...</b>

22:17.020 --> 22:18.380
<b>Please...</b>

22:45.910 --> 22:48.310
<b>Bun... chan...</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.970 --> 24:22.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:20.910 --> 24:22.070
<b>My voice is all gargly.</b>

24:22.070 --> 24:24.210
<b>Huh? Taruto chan, you sound terrible!</b>

24:24.210 --> 24:27.040
<b>Yeah, I coughed too much and
my voice turned into this.</b>

24:27.050 --> 24:28.910
<b>Your voice also sounds different, Rokkun.</b>

24:28.910 --> 24:30.180
<b>I just caught a light cold.</b>

24:30.180 --> 24:32.980
<b>That sounds pretty bad.
Huh? Speaking of which, where’s Grandma?</b>

24:32.980 --> 24:34.850
<b>I heard Old Lady Okaka also caught a cold.</b>

24:34.850 --> 24:36.550
<b>Here I am!</b>

24:36.560 --> 24:39.020
<b>What happened?
Your voice is way too different.</b>

24:39.020 --> 24:41.230
<b>Yeah, yeah. For some reason, it
sounds so sweet and soothing.</b>

24:41.230 --> 24:44.230
<b>It sounds like the chirping of young
birds flying around a lake.</b>

24:44.230 --> 24:46.660
<b>Really? I think it’s pretty much the same as normal...</b>

24:46.670 --> 24:49.270
<b>Well, I think I’ll do the preview quickly
today so I can hurry on home.</b>

24:49.270 --> 24:51.340
<b>After all, I have a big mountain-climbing
adventure with the elderly club!</b>

24:51.340 --> 24:52.600
<b>How completely out of place...</b>

24:52.600 --> 24:54.940
<b>Stop saying such things with that voice!</b>

24:54.940 --> 24:55.910
<b>Be quiet!</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>Material Fairies</b>

24:55.910 --> 24:58.080
<b>Next time: “Material Fairies.”</b>
